  "names": {
    "order": "given family family",
    "conventions": "Chileans carry two surnames, the father's first and the mother's second (Josefa Muñoz Rojas), and both are used on forms, at school and at work. Two given names are usual too (José Tomás, María Ignacia). Popular names lean classic: Agustín, Benjamín, Vicente, Isidora, Josefa, Trinidad, Antonia. González and Muñoz top the surname list. Mapuche families carry surnames from Mapudungun (Painemal, Catrileo, Huenchullán) and sometimes Mapuche given names like Rayén or Millaray. Santiago also has large Venezuelan, Peruvian and Haitian communities.",
